WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.480
- But tell us how, so
why did you adopt first?

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.900
Your adopted first, right?

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.733
- We did.

00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:08.220
I'd always talked about
adopting my whole life.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.200
My mom is actually adopted

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.130
and I just thought it was really cool.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.640
And so we talked about it off and on,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.380
but it wasn't something
that we had sat down

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.893
and had like a full on
adoption conversation.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.960
And then I was in Uganda in 2016.

00:00:26.288 --> 00:00:27.121
- Yeah.

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:31.200
- And I had a picture of
one of the babies there,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.080
and I had shared it on social media.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.580
And when I finally got to
FaceTime him that night,

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.170
I was telling him our story

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.797
and I was like, "Babe,
we know so many people

00:00:42.797 --> 00:00:45.057
"who are trying to adopt right now

00:00:45.057 --> 00:00:48.545
"and this little girl
needs a forever home."

00:00:48.545 --> 00:00:51.470
And I was like so moved.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:54.860
I mean, the second I touched
her it was like electric.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.077
And I was like, "Oh my word.

00:00:56.077 --> 00:00:58.980
"This little girl has
just taken my heart."

00:00:58.980 --> 00:00:59.927
And I was like,

00:00:59.927 --> 00:01:02.127
"Honey, we've got to find
her her forever home,

00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:03.637
"like I know that's why I'm here,

00:01:03.637 --> 00:01:06.270
"is to get this girl to her home."

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.697
And--

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:09.280
- Oh my God, okay.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.300
(all laugh)

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:14.320
That totally opered me
just now like, okay.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.180
I did my own makeup and, I
mean, this is not waterproof.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.560
(laughs)

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.520
Like, it's so beautiful
'cause I know that feeling

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.080
because I'm only, you
touch me, you hold to me.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.070
It doesn't matter if it's yours or not.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.320
We're a blended family in your life.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.430
This is my purpose.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.730
It's such a powerful thing.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.563
- Yeah, for sure.

00:01:31.563 --> 00:01:34.570
- So how did that turn
into y'all adopting?

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.200
- Well, just out of the blue.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.470
- When I talked to her
on the phone that night

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.920
and she said that we need to
find her a home, I literally...

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.500
It was after a concert
and I was going to bed

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.070
and I was like, "Well, bring her home."

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.620
And I don't fully remember even saying it.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.520
Like it was like such a
spiritual thing for me

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.070
that it just came out of my body,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.550
and then literally two
weeks after we were having,

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.350
you know, home assessments and talking

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.060
to adoption agencies and...

